{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>In the grave which I hewed for myself.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'I hewed' — from the root of (Exodus 21): ״כי יכרה איש בור״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: כריתי — from the root of כרי (heap). Jacob took silver and gold, made of it a great heap, and gave it to Esau, saying to him: 'Take it in exchange for your portion in the cave.' And this is אשר כריתי לי — that is, which I acquired for myself with the money of the heap."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:51.716300999Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}